From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:57:52 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: Markdown files get the composer's block look and
 quotation highlight

Operator, 2026-11-22: the highlight "has to exist in the editor's content
area too; today it is only in the agent panel" -- and, asked to confirm,
the same behaviour as the composer in Markdown files. An editor showing
one Markdown file now gets what the composer has: fenced code and `>`
quotes look like blocks (0107), text in quotation marks is highlighted
(0122), and a typed backtick fence closes itself (0107, 0153).

markdown_file_look.rs (new) runs the composer's own functions --
composer_blocks::refresh_composer_blocks and close_opened_fence -- so the
composer and the files cannot drift apart; only the trigger is new.
agent_ui::init registers an observer on every new full editor, which
subscribes to that editor's events:
- Reparsed refreshes the look. The editor emits it after the parse that
  follows each edit and on a language change, which is also the moment a
  file's language becomes known after it opens. BufferEdited as well
  would rescan the whole text twice per keystroke.
- InputHandled ending in a backtick runs the fence rule.
Only a singleton buffer with a file, in Markdown, at most 1 MiB
(MARKDOWN_FILE_LOOK_MAX_BYTES), is handled. The file is what keeps the
composer out: it is a Markdown buffer with none, in a full editor while
empty or expanded, and it closes its fences itself, so handling it here
would close a fence twice.

Known gaps: a file over the limit keeps upstream's look (every edit
rescans the whole text); a file whose language stops being Markdown, by a
rename, keeps its last look until it is reopened.

Tests: markdown_file_look::tests, 4 GPUI -- a Markdown file gets the code
rows, the quote rows and the quotation background and follows an edit; a
fence typed in a file closes as long as it is (0153); a .txt file keeps
upstream's look; a Markdown buffer with no file is left alone (the
composer's guard). Red seen with init returning early: the first two
failed, the two guards passed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---

diff --git a/crates/agent_ui/src/agent_ui.rs b/crates/agent_ui/src/agent_ui.rs
index ddee24f..0ef3979 100644
